Content: what zebkit's automation needs that the public API does not give.

zebkit runs Playwright's API inside the engine, without DevTools
(docs/AUTOMATION.md). Four things it needs are content's own, which only
its DevTools handlers reach; content/public/browser/zebkit_automation.h
gives them to the embedder, in one new file:

- the widget under a point of a page, a frame of another site's included,
  and the point in it (GetRenderWidgetHostAtPointAsynchronously), so that
  mouse input reaches the frame a person's would, as DevTools' Input
  domain sends it;
- touch events to a widget (RenderInputRouter::ForwardTouchEventWithLatencyInfo);
- the position a page's Geolocation API reads (Playwright's
  setGeolocation; DevTools' Emulation.setGeolocationOverride);
- a frame's subresource loader factories made again, so that the
  embedder's factory is in front of the network's from now on, as
  DevTools' Fetch domain does when it starts.

